Z||000000||Kasdan||11-10-2001||12:23 AM||||Hey people, i raced a 1985 Ferrari Mondial 3.2 on Atlanta Highway here in Athens...and won.  It was some old woman driving it, i think she was in like her 40's (not old, i know, but im 17).  I had her by like 1/2 a car length, like 1/8th mile run.  it was an insanely nice car...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1985_ferrari_mondial_32-1.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>Tyler Morgan, 1986 GT<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero21.jpg">               <BR>Aftermarket Power Steering, Rebuilt motor with &gt;100 miles, Aim=FieroDriver1986||||reg||1
Z||000001||Kasdan||11-10-2001||12:24 AM||||It was black, and yes, she WAS pulling on me, she would have had me in the 1/4th.||||reg||1
Z||000002||artherd||11-10-2001||12:32 AM||||Coooooool man!!<P>They're really nice cars, got to drive a friend's 3.2 Mondial Cabriolet once.  Wind in hair, Ferrari 4-cam V8 in back, gated shifter clacking devinely...  Life is good!!!<P>PS: don't think she knew how to drive it, that V8 is a peaky motor and loves to be reved  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  It'd eat my Formula for lunch.  (145 in a convertible is *scary*  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000003||Kasdan||11-10-2001||12:34 AM||||Yeah,  i know she didnt know how to drive it (obviously), and no im not lieing, i really did beat her, i just dont want this to turn into a flame war...||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||11-10-2001||04:39 AM||||The Mondial is one of the worse looking, worse performing Ferraris made after the 40's. Ferraris attempt at making a more family friendly car. There resale value will tell you their the least desireable of all. They have the same drivetrain as 308/328 basicly and dragging around the extra weight. and like all euro sports cars, they love revs for power. She prob just left it in high gear and stomped it. I downshift whenever i need to, to pass, at anything usually under around 90. still though a kills a kill. If you gunfight a guy with a 357 and you have a 38, if you get him first, hes still just as dead.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroMontreal||11-10-2001||01:05 PM||||Maybe it was a dressed up fiero...? <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigfieromontreal_1.gif"> <BR>1986 Fiero GT, STOCK Wingless, <BR>-Alex President of FieroMontreal... <A HREF="http://www.fieromontreal.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieromontreal.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Formula88||11-10-2001||03:44 PM||||Good kill!  Whether you had the more powerful car, or the more skillful driver doesn't matter.  Good job.<P>That's like when LZeitgeist and I race.  We have virtually identical Formulas.  Both 5 speeds, etc.  The only difference is I have A/C and he doesn't (and I weight more than his scrawny self).  So he's got a weight advantage of maybe 100-200 lbs over me.  Still, every race we've been in has almost always been decided by driver skill.  When we both cut good launches and nail the shifts, we run almost exactly dead even.  As it should be in identical cars.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I think I may be making slightly more power to be able to keep up with my weight disadvantage, but that's probably because I have a RAM clutch and his is an OEM replacement, and I have a hi-flow cat to his OEM cat.  I think we're changing his clutch next spring.<P>I tell you, you want excitement - race a car that's almost identical.  THEN it's a race.  One slip and you've lost.  That get's the adrenaline flowing!!||||reg||14
Z||000007||kempo||11-10-2001||08:16 PM||||Most older Ferrari times in 0-60 aren't real impressive.  Say a 1983 308 0-60 in about 7.7 seconds.  The catch is, after 60mph, they out perform the energizer bunny, and keep on going and going and going, and at a faster rate of acceleration than other cars...  Ahh, the joys of driving sports cars!  Good kill!<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.admist.net/gtsmall.jpg">    <BR>0-60 6.9 seconds||||reg||1
Z||000008||Gerald||11-10-2001||08:20 PM||||Nice kill. Ummm I beat a ford areostar. I feel dumb now||||reg||1
Z||000009||Seanh||11-10-2001||08:30 PM||||Sounds like a sweet race. I hate racing when I get my doors blown off, or I just totally destroy the other car, its no fun. I like racing when the cars are side by side and you look over and see everything else flying by and the car staying right next to you. I raced a 5spd 3.1 aluminum headed beretta last night and it was a nice race. I would have beat it in the 1/4, but we didn't mark off any track or anything, and she did take me in the upper end cuz I only had the 3spd auto now. Thru my 1st and 2nd gears I had her pretty good, but when I hit 3rd my cars done for, if I don't have enough distance by then I'm screwed.<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly - 86 GT<BR>Back to my 3.1L...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Image2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Jay||11-10-2001||09:40 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B>The Mondial is one of the worse looking, worse performing Ferraris made after the 40's. Ferraris attempt at making a more family friendly car. There resale value will tell you their the least desireable of all.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>What is bad looking about this?<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mondial.jpg"> <BR>  I've driven one for an entire week-end and plan on buying one in the near future.  It's not ment to be a sports car, it's a 2+2 grand tourer that replaced the 400i and 412i.  I got that baby up to 180km/hr and there is no way a fiero could beat it, if it were really trying.  In 5th it could still snap your neck back if you stomped on it.  Still, It's nice to believe that you could <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  The fact that resale is low means you can pick up a great car for relatively cheap...If you consider $40-50 000 cheap for a 20 year old car.  Prices are even higher if it is a Mondial T.<P><P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsig2_copy_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||rogergarrison||11-10-2001||09:59 PM||||dont get me wrong jay, i love all Ferraris. The mondial is great for a family car (2 kid seats in back) But they stretched the wheelbase in front of rear wheels (made it more squirrely than 308/328). Also moved the windshield and front seats farther forward. that moved balance too far forward. You feel almost like your sitting on the front wheels (ie minivan)Anyway with all that, it just dont look sleek anymore, looks like a station wagon with the top cut off. There usually dirt cheap used, as Ferraris go. The recent pic of the yellow Fiero with the stock body stretched comes to mind. You can find them in pretty decent shape for less than $20 K.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 11-10-2001).]||||reg||1
